{
    "background_story": "Dashing was a majestic stallion with a coat as black as coal and a mane that shone like gold. He was known for his incredible speed and agility, but what set him apart was his unique ability to divide his attention into perfect aliquots. Whether he was competing in a high-stakes tournament or simply grazing in the pasture, Dashing could focus on multiple things at once with uncanny precision. His rider, a young jockey named Emma, marveled at how Dashing could simultaneously respond to her subtle cues, navigate treacherous terrain, and adjust his stride to optimize their performance. As they galloped across the finish line, Emma would often whisper, 'You're a true mathematician, Dashing!' - a testament to the horse's remarkable ability to divide his attention into perfect, harmonious parts.",
